# Higher Education Finance and Economic Inequality in Greece.

**Authors:** Patrinos, Harry Anthony

## Abstract
Examines equity aspects of Greek &quot;free&quot; higher education by analyzing differential benefits and costs of public subsidization and by determining individual benefits of education by social origin. Finds that the poor pay proportionately more for schooling (through taxes) and receive less in terms of educational attainment and educational subsidies. (SV)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ450624

